❓Question:
Given two sorted arrays nums1 and nums2, merge nums2 into nums1 so that the final array is also sorted in non-decreasing order.
nums1 already has enough extra space to store all elements of nums2.

✅Approach:
First, copy all elements of nums2 into the empty positions at the end of nums1. Then use Arrays.sort(nums1) to sort the complete array.

Code:
class Solution {
    public void merge(int[] nums1, int m, int[] nums2, int n) {
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            nums1[m + i] = nums2[i];
        }
        Arrays.sort(nums1);
    }
}
Time Complexity: O((m+n) log(m+n))
Space Complexity: O(log(m+n)) due to sorting.
